  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f22f57d0cf5c493280a0ab6b7dbaea9e3fc5b035c6d410d59c2f476043bd03a8.png] \n\nGiven equation:\n\n10 ÷ 6 × 4 + 14 − 24 = 30\n\nChecking options one by one by interchanging the numbers and applying the BODMAS rule:-\n\noption 1)** **4, 6\n\n**__10 ÷ 4__ **× 6** **+ 14 − 24 = 30\n\n__**2.5 × 6**__ + 14 - 24 = 30\n\n__**15 + 14**__ - 24 = 30\n\n29 - 24 = 30\n\n5 ≠ 30\n\noption 2) 10, 6\n\n__**6 ÷ 10**__ × 4 + 14 - 24 = 30\n\n__**0.6 × 4**__ + 14 - 24 = 30\n\n__**2.4 + 14**__ - 24 = 30\n\n16.4 - 24 = 30\n\n-7.6 ≠ 30\n\noption 3) 14, 24\n\n__**10 ÷ 6**__ × 4 + 24 - 14 = 30\n\n__**1.66 × 4**__ + 24 - 14 = 30\n\n__**6.64 + 24**__ - 14 = 30\n\n30.64 - 14 = 30\n\n16.64 ≠ 30\n\noption 4) 10, 30\n\n__**30 ÷ 6**__ × 4 + 14 - 24 = 10\n\n**__5 × 4__** + 14 - 24 = 10\n\n__**20 + 14**__ - 24 = 10\n\n34 - 24 = 10\n\n10 = 10 (Left hand side = Right hand side)\n\nHence, the correct pair of numbers that satisfies the equation is \"**(10, 30)**\"**.**",
